{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>When they journeyed</b> — Two times in the Masorah: בנסעם מן המחנה / בנסעם מקדם. There below (they) rebelled; here too (they) rebelled.\n\nHe made inverted nuns, for he wanted to bring across the tribes whose letters are nun across the Jordan, which is fifty [mil] wide, but their sin caused [otherwise].\n\nAnother reason for the inverted nuns, as stated in Shabbat, chapter Kol Kitvei: this is not its place, and it was written here to separate between the first punishment and the second punishment. And he made inverted nuns for the nun, whose place is before the three parashiyot before it — and were the nuns not inverted, I would not know whether [it refers] to after nun parashiyot or before nun parashiyot. Therefore he made them inverted, to say: before nun, before it. And that is after ונסע אהל מועד מחנה הלוים, in the portion BaMidbar, for from there until here is nun [50] parashiyot."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The opening juxtaposition reads בנסעם מן המחנה against בנסעם מקדם; the latter phrase does not appear in the canonical text of Numbers 10:35, which reads ויהי בנסע הארון. The phrase may reflect a variant reading or a masoretic notation; translated as found."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:50.472497513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}